\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,c(x)=-1,$ and $f(x)=1.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{′}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)={x}^{2},$ and $f(x)={e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$; $x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186464871 :answer-field/key "I" "$2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$"] [:db/cas 17592186464872 :answer-field/key "II" "${y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186464873 :answer-field/key "III" "$x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$"] [:db/cas 17592186265954 :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** $(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2$\n- **II.** ${y}^{3}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-xy=0$\n- **III.** $\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+xy{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186265954 :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,b(x)=-x,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)=2.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-xy=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{3}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+xy{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $xy{y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,b(x)=-x,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)=2.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-xy=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{3}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+xy{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $xy{y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186464874 :answer-field/key "I" "$(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2$"] [:db/cas 17592186464875 :answer-field/key "II" "${y}^{3}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-xy=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186464876 :answer-field/key "III" "$\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+xy{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$"] [:db/cas 17592186265955 :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** ${e}^{2y}{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+3=0$\n- **II.** ${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+5y=x$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186265955 :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{2y}{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+3=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${e}^{2y}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=4,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=2+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+5y=x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=-2x,c(x)=5,$ and $f(x)=x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{2y}{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+3=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${e}^{2y}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=4,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=2+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+5y=x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=-2x,c(x)=5,$ and $f(x)=x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2$; ${y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+5y=x$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186464877 :answer-field/key "I" "${e}^{2y}{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+3=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186464878 :answer-field/key "II" "${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2$"] [:db/cas 17592186464879 :answer-field/key "III" "${y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+5y=x$"] [:db/cas 17592186265956 :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** $2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,{y}^{′}+{y}^{2}=0$\n- **II.** $2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186265956 :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,{y}^{′}+{y}^{2}=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)={x}^{3},c(x)=2x,$ and $f(x)=0.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=x,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=x{e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,{y}^{′}+{y}^{2}=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)={x}^{3},c(x)=2x,$ and $f(x)=0.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=x,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=x{e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0$; ${y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186464880 :answer-field/key "I" "$2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,{y}^{′}+{y}^{2}=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186464881 :answer-field/key "II" "$2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186464882 :answer-field/key "III" "${y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}$"] [:db/cas 17592186265973 :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186464883 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464884 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464885 :answer-field/key "C" "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186265998 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186464886 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464887 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464888 :answer-field/key "C" "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186266034 :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-3x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{4x}$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-12y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n- **I.** $y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{{e}^{-3x}}$\n- **II.** $y(x)={e}^{4x}+{e}^{-3x}$\n- **III.** $y(x)={e}^{x}$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-3x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{4x}$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-12y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186266034 :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{{e}^{-3x}}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotients of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)={e}^{4x}+{e}^{-3x}$ 